WEBVTT

00:00.650 --> 00:01.850
We're asked to subtract.

00:01.850 --> 00:04.710
And we have the complex
number 2 minus 3i.

00:04.710 --> 00:09.420
And from that, we are
subtracting 6 minus 18i.

00:09.420 --> 00:11.070
So the first thing
I'd like to do here

00:11.070 --> 00:13.620
is to just get rid
of these parentheses.

00:13.620 --> 00:16.379
So we just have a bunch of
real parts and imaginary parts

00:16.379 --> 00:18.150
that we can then
add up together.

00:18.150 --> 00:21.140
So we have 2 minus 3i.

00:21.140 --> 00:23.590
And then we're subtracting
this entire quantity.

00:23.590 --> 00:25.020
And to get rid of
the parentheses,

00:25.020 --> 00:26.960
we can just distribute
the negative sign.

00:26.960 --> 00:28.334
Or another way to
think about it,

00:28.334 --> 00:31.097
we can say that this is
negative 1 times all of this.

00:31.097 --> 00:32.930
So we can just distribute
the negative sign.

00:32.930 --> 00:37.470
And negative 1 times
6 is negative 6.

00:37.470 --> 00:39.470
Let me do these in magenta.

00:39.470 --> 00:41.340
So this is negative 6.

00:41.340 --> 00:44.290
And then negative 1 times
negative 18i-- well, that's

00:44.290 --> 00:47.260
just going to be positive 18i.

00:47.260 --> 00:50.010
Negative times a
negative is a positive.

00:50.010 --> 00:51.740
And now we want to
add the real parts,

00:51.740 --> 00:54.300
and we want to add
the imaginary parts.

00:54.300 --> 00:56.630
So here's a real part here, 2.

00:56.630 --> 00:58.360
And then we have a minus 6.

00:58.360 --> 01:00.260
So we have 2 minus 6.

01:00.260 --> 01:02.460
And we want to add
the imaginary parts.

01:02.460 --> 01:04.019
We have a negative.

01:04.019 --> 01:05.570
Let me do that in
a different color.

01:05.570 --> 01:09.370
We have a negative
3i right over here.

01:09.370 --> 01:12.550
So negative 3i, or minus
3i right over there.

01:12.550 --> 01:15.120
And then we have a plus
18i or positive 18i.

01:18.570 --> 01:23.950
If you add the real parts,
2 minus 6 is negative 4.

01:23.950 --> 01:27.320
And you add the imaginary parts.

01:27.320 --> 01:29.160
If I have negative
3 of something

01:29.160 --> 01:31.367
and to that I add
18 of something,

01:31.367 --> 01:33.950
well, that's just going to leave
me with 15 of that something.

01:33.950 --> 01:34.860
Or another way you
could think about it,

01:34.860 --> 01:38.060
if I have 18 of something and
I subtract 3 of that something,

01:38.060 --> 01:39.850
I'll have 15 of that something.

01:39.850 --> 01:44.620
And in this case, the something
is i, is the imaginary unit.

01:44.620 --> 01:47.700
So this is going to be plus 15i.

01:50.560 --> 01:53.140
And we are done.
